The adoption of AI, however, has led to various concerns, such as consumer trust, interactions, and perceived risk, which have a direct influence on effective relationship management between consumers and organizations (Hsiao & Chen, 2021). Hasan et al. (2021) find that consumers often feel conflicted on whether they should adopt new technologies due to trust, ethics, data collection, usage, and privacy issues, especially after the Facebook data breach in 2018. This incident involved more than 50 million users’ data harvested for third parties, and it has significantly impacted people’s trust in online platforms used for mostly non-commercial activities (Hasan et al., 2021; Landwehr, 2019; Liyanaarachchi et al., 2020). Yen & Chiang (2021) believe that even though the use of AI is on the rise, organizations need to focus on building trust with consumers and assure them that their privacy and personal information

